        description="Different creative angles produced different responses. Desire was particularly effective at generating initial response for Terrace Garden, while Testimonial demonstrated its ability to generate leads after Desire was removed." 
      />
      <InsightCard 
        category="Insight 2" 
        title="Conversion design should match the service" 
        description="I did not force both services into the same conversion mechanism: Terrace Garden used Instant Forms for structured qualification, while Interior Design used WhatsApp for direct communication." 
      />
      <InsightCard 
        category="Insight 3" 
        title="Performance data isn't the only constraint" 
        description="Desire was performing well, but it still had to be removed because of a business/usage constraint. The highest-performing creative isn't always the creative you are allowed to keep running." 
      />
      <InsightCard 
        category="Insight 4" 
        title="Avoid unnecessary intervention" 
        description="After Desire was removed, I did not immediately restructure the campaign or make multiple simultaneous changes. The remaining Testimonial creative subsequently began producing leads." 
      />
